<section class="sx-section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
  <div class="sx-wrap">
    <p class="sx-kicker">Selected work</p>
    <h2 id="work-title">Case studies</h2>
    <p class="sx-sub">Self-initiated and internship projects. Open any one for the full story.</p>
    <div class="project-grid sx-projects">
<a class="workspace-card card-studybuddy" href="case-studies/study-buddy.html" data-case-study="Study Buddy">
            <div class="card-art"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/images/study-buddy.png" alt="Study Buddy desktop focus companion app"></div>
            <div class="card-details">
              <div class="card-title"><div><h2>Study Buddy — Desktop Focus Companion</h2></div></div>
              <strong class="card-role">Solo Product Designer</strong>
              <div class="card-tags"><span>Desktop App (Windows / Mac / Linux)</span><span>Design Systems</span><span>AI-Assisted Build</span><span>Interactive Overlay</span><span>WCAG AA</span></div>
              <p class="card-problem"><b>Problem:</b> Unstructured study sessions lead to digital distraction, while rigid timers disrupt deep focus.</p>
              <p>Designed a floating desktop overlay in Figma, then built and shipped cross-platform installers by directing AI through staged commits.</p>
              <p class="card-outcome"><b>Outcome:</b> Shipped working installers across 3 operating systems in ~14 hours of build time. Dogfooded daily to eliminate edge cases.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
<a class="workspace-card card-secureid" href="case-studies/secureid.html" data-case-study="SecureID">
            <div class="card-art"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/images/secureid.png" alt="SecureID identity-verification flow and analyst dashboard"></div>
            <div class="card-details">
              <div class="card-title"><div><h2>SecureID — Identity Verification &amp; Analyst Review Platform</h2></div></div>
              <strong class="card-role">Solo Product Designer</strong>
              <div class="card-tags"><span>Dual-Sided: Mobile &amp; SaaS Dashboard</span><span>Design Tokens</span><span>Clickable Prototype</span><span>Case Triage UX</span><span>Progressive Disclosure</span></div>
              <p class="card-problem"><b>Problem:</b> Anxious mobile users faced verification drop-off, while fraud analysts struggled with cluttered review queues.</p>
              <p>Designed an end-user mobile verification journey and a high-throughput desktop analyst dashboard on 1 unified token architecture.</p>
              <p class="card-outcome"><b>Outcome:</b> 1 shared token system across mobile &amp; web, a 3-action analyst triage pattern (Approve, Escalate, Reject), and a verified Figma prototype.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
<a class="workspace-card card-vextaro" href="case-studies/vextaro.html" data-case-study="Vextaro">
            <div class="card-art"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/images/vextaro.png" alt="Vextaro luxury formalwear rental app"></div>
            <div class="card-details">
              <div class="card-title"><div><h2>Vextaro — Luxury Formalwear Rental App &amp; System</h2></div></div>
              <strong class="card-role">UX/UI Design Intern · Flyrank AI</strong>
              <div class="card-tags"><span>Mobile App (iOS &amp; Android)</span><span>Design Systems &amp; Tokens</span><span>UX Research &amp; IA</span><span>WCAG 2.2 AA Audit</span><span>Engineering Handoff</span></div>
              <p class="card-problem"><b>Problem:</b> Renters cannot try formalwear on before it ships, making fit uncertainty the #1 checkout blocker.</p>
              <p>Led competitive research to design a specialist fit-confirmation checkpoint, tokenized UI system, and an accessible high-fidelity prototype.</p>
              <p class="card-outcome"><b>Outcome:</b> 7-section IA, 15/15 WCAG AA contrast checks passed, 35 component variants documented, and a developer-ready handoff package.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
<a class="workspace-card card-honda" href="case-studies/honda.html" data-case-study="Honda of Clear Lake">
            <div class="card-art"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/images/honda.png" alt="Honda of Clear Lake website heuristic evaluation"></div>
            <div class="card-details">
              <div class="card-title"><div><h2>Honda of Clear Lake — Dealership Website Usability Audit</h2></div></div>
              <strong class="card-role">Solo UX Auditor</strong>
              <div class="card-tags"><span>Responsive Dealership Website</span><span>Heuristic Evaluation</span><span>Nielsen's 10 Heuristics</span><span>Severity Rating (0–4)</span><span>Conversion Optimization</span></div>
              <p class="card-problem"><b>Problem:</b> Car buyers experienced severe friction finding real-time pricing, trade-in values, and financing terms.</p>
              <p>Audited the live dealership site against Nielsen's 10 heuristics, identifying 31 usability violations across core conversion paths.</p>
              <p class="card-outcome"><b>Outcome:</b> Ranked findings on a 0–4 severity scale with annotated redesign proposals and an engineering punch list for 3 critical blockers.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
<a class="workspace-card card-devtective" href="case-studies/devtective.html" data-case-study="DevTective">
            <div class="card-art"><img loading="lazy" src="assets/images/devtective.png" alt="DevTective coding progress tracker app"></div>
            <div class="card-details">
              <div class="card-title"><div><h2>DevTective — Developer Learning Progress &amp; Habit Tracker</h2></div></div>
              <strong class="card-role">Solo UX Designer</strong>
              <div class="card-tags"><span>Mobile Web App</span><span>Google UX Certificate</span><span>User Research</span><span>Journey Mapping</span><span>Wireframe to Prototype</span></div>
              <p class="card-problem"><b>Problem:</b> Self-taught coders face high drop-off rates due to cognitive overload and lack of structured milestone tracking.</p>
              <p>Conducted user interviews, mapped emotional journeys, and designed low-to-high fidelity flows to help beginners sustain daily learning habits.</p>
              <p class="card-outcome"><b>Outcome:</b> Completed end-to-end UX research foundation, personas, wireframes, and responsive interactive prototype.</p>
            </div>
          </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sx-section" id="experience" aria-labelledby="exp-title">
  <div class="sx-wrap">
    <p class="sx-kicker">Experience</p>
    <h2 id="exp-title">Two design internships, running in parallel</h2>
    <div class="sx-exp">
      <article class="sx-exp-card">
        <header>
          <h3>Product Design Intern</h3>
          <p>Stealth Startup · Jul 2026 – Present · Remote</p>
        </header>
        <ul class="hero-bullets">
          <li><strong>End-to-End System Creation:</strong> Led a token-based Figma system from scratch across 2 mobile apps and a desktop dashboard as 1 of ~5 design interns.</li>
          <li><strong>High-Fidelity Prototyping:</strong> Built complex prototypes with conditional logic and typeable fields, saving 30+ minutes of setup per founder demo.</li>
          <li><strong>Feature Delivery:</strong> Designed and handed off ~30 responsive screens and modal overlays collaborating directly with engineering and founders.</li>
          <li><strong>Mentorship &amp; Workshops:</strong> Mentored 2–3 design interns per session and led monthly Figma workshops on Auto Layout and variables.</li>
          <li class="hero-note">Under NDA; company details confidential.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="sx-exp-card">
        <header>
          <h3>UI/UX Design Intern</h3>
          <p>Flyrank AI · Jul 2026 – Nov 2026 · Remote</p>
        </header>
        <ul class="hero-bullets">
          <li><strong>Design Systems Architecture:</strong> Built a centralized Figma token system (variables, 4-color semantic palette, type scale), eliminating per-screen rework across mobile and web.</li>
          <li><strong>User Research &amp; Checkpoint:</strong> Synthesized 10+ competitive audits into a pre-checkout fit-confirmation checkpoint to resolve rental sizing anxiety.</li>
          <li><strong>Accessibility &amp; Design QA:</strong> Audited 15 checks against WCAG 2.2 AA at the token level, resolving text contrast (4.29:1 → 8.31:1) and touch target sizes.</li>
          <li><strong>Engineering Handoff:</strong> Documented 35 component variants, annotated redlines, and 146 interactive prototype connections for developer handoff.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sx-section" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
  <div class="sx-wrap">
    <p class="sx-kicker">How I work</p>
    <h2 id="process-title">Fast, with a human in the loop.</h2>
    <p class="sx-sub">My AI-assisted process, with Study Buddy as the example.</p>
    <ol class="hero-flow hero-map"><li><b>01</b><strong>Design first</strong><span>I design the product in Figma before any code exists.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> a floating desktop focus companion, designed screen by screen.</em></li><li><b>02</b><strong>Write staged change lists</strong><span>I break the build into small, ordered requests for the AI.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> the app was built in stages, one change list at a time.</em></li><li><b>03</b><strong>AI builds a round</strong><span>The AI writes the code for that stage.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> Electron, React, and TypeScript across 40+ commits.</em></li><li><b>04</b><strong>Review against designs</strong><span>I check every round against my Figma designs.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> each round compared with the original screens.</em></li><li><b>05</b><strong>Decide and correct</strong><span>I cut, fix, and redirect what does not hold up.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> cut features, fixed contrast failures, changed window behavior.</em></li><li><b>06</b><strong>Ship</strong><span>I repeat steps 3 to 5 until it is ready to use.</span><em><i>Study Buddy:</i> about 14 hours of active build time; Windows, Mac, and Linux installers.</em></li></ol>
    <p class="hero-flow-tools">I use AI to move quickly and stay accountable for what ships. Build time counted from commit timestamps.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sx-section" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title">
  <div class="sx-wrap">
    <p class="sx-kicker">Skills and tools</p>
    <h2 id="skills-title">From research to engineering handoff</h2>
    <ol class="hero-flow"><li><b>01 · Understand</b><span>UX research</span><span>Usability testing</span><span>Information architecture</span><span>User flows</span></li><li><b>02 · Systematize</b><span>Design systems</span><span>Tokens &amp; variables</span><span>Responsive design</span><span>WCAG accessibility</span></li><li><b>03 · Prototype</b><span>Wireframing</span><span>Interactive prototyping</span><span>Figma</span><span>HTML &amp; CSS</span></li><li><b>04 · Hand off</b><span>Engineering handoff</span><span>Specs &amp; annotations</span><span>AI-assisted React &amp; TypeScript</span></li></ol>
    <p class="hero-flow-tools">AI in my workflow: Claude, Gemini, GitHub Copilot, Granola AI. Every output reviewed against user needs.</p>
  </div>
</section>

